<lines>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_1">¶//Priusquam ad diuisionem pretij ve¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_2">niamus, definiendū est nobis pre¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_3">tium in genere, licet in nullo Doctore</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_4">eius repererim definitionem. //Pretium</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_5">&amp; latissimè dicitur, &amp; strictè: latissime</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_6">dictum transcendit nostrum propositū,</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_7">&amp; materiam emptionum, &amp; venditio¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_8">num, de qua agimus, &amp; inuenitur in</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_9">omnibus rebus tam materialibus, quam</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_10">spiritualibus, &amp; nihil est aliud, quàm</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_11">aestimatio cuiusque rei. //Quae aestimatio</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_12">est rectum iudicium rerum, quo alias</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_13">alijs conferentes, &amp; quasi iudicij nostri</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_14">fidelis trutina ponderantes alias alijs,</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_15">vel postponimus, vel praeponimus, vel</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_16">aequamus secundum cuiuscumque rei</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_17">meritum, &amp; dignitatem. //Sicut enim</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_18">is, qui aequa lance propendit rerū pon¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_19">dera, &amp; momenta, ad {dignoſendum|dignoscendum}</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_20">pretium, &amp; pondus eius, alijs ponderi¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_21">bus rem illam praeponit, alijs postponit,</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_22">alijs coęquat, ijs scilicet, quae tantundem</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_23">valoris habent. //Ita nos iudicio nostro</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_24">res aestimantes ponderantes, ac truti¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_25">nantes alias alijs postponimus, alias an¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_26">teferimus, alias coaequamus; &amp; illud</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_27">iudicium, quo eas aestimamus, est pre¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_28">tium, in quo easdem res habemus, &amp;</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_29">hoc modo tot sunt pretia rerum, quot</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_30">sunt hominum, immo &amp; Angelorum</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_31">&amp; ipsius Dei iudicia de illis. //Hac diffe¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_32">rentia obseruata, quod iudicium Dei in</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_33">rerum ęstimatione semper est verum,</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_34">semper ęquum, semper nostrorum iudi¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_35">ciorum, &amp; appretiationum metrum, &amp;</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_36">mensura: iudicium verò, &amp; pretium ho¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_37">minum fallax est, &amp; mendax, quia men¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_38">daces filij hominum in stateris suis.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_39">¶//Sicut autem iustitia specialis commu¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_40">tatiua consistit in recta ponderatione</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_41">rerum mensurabilium cum pretio, ita ut</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_42">nec magis, nec minus detur in pretio,</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_43">sed omnino ęquale, cum verò earum</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_44">pondere. //Ita iustitia vniuersalis, quae</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_45">omnem virtutem complectitur cōsistit</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_46">in vera earum aestimatione, qua vnam¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_47">quamque rerum omnium vera trutina,</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_48">&amp; aequa lance pensitantes, nec magis,</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_49">nec minus aestimamus, sed ęqualiter ad</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_50">{amuſim|amussim}, ac vt recta ratio exigit ei prae¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_51">ponentes quae praeferenda secundū re¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_52">ctam rationem sunt, &amp; postponentes</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_53">quę postponenda sunt, &amp; aequantes, quę</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_54">sunt coaequanda. //Sic Magnus Augustinus</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_55">acutissimè, &amp; sanctissimè dixit: [Ille iu¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_56">stè, &amp; sanctè viuit, qui rerum integer ae¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_57">stimator est, ipse est, qui ordinatam ha¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_58">bet charitatem, vt non magis diligat,</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_59">quod minus diligendum est, nec minus</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_60">diligat, quod magis diligendum est, nec</line>
</lines>
